      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve for \\( b \\), we need to first solve for \\( x \\) in the first equation and then use that value in the second equation to solve for \\( b \\).\n\nFrom the first equation \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\):\n1. Subtract 7 from both sides: \\( 2x = 3 - 7 \\)\n2. Simplify the right side: \\( 2x = -4 \\)\n3. Divide both sides by 2: \\( x = -4 / 2 \\)\n4. Simplify the right side: \\( x = -2 \\)\n\nNow that we know \\( x = -2 \\) from the first equation, we use this value in the second equation \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\):\n1. Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the second equation: \\( b(-2) - 10 = -2 \\)\n2. Distribute the \\( b \\): \\( -2b - 10 = -2 \\)\n3. Add 10 to both sides: \\( -2b = -2 + 10 \\)\n4. Simplify the right side: \\( -2b = 8 \\)\n5. Divide both sides by -2: \\( b = 8 / -2 \\)\n6. Simplify the right side: \\( b = -4 \\)\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
