      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's first solve for $x$ in the first equation $2x+7=3$. Subtracting 7 from both sides gives $2x = -4$. Dividing both sides by 2 then gets us $x = -2$ as our value of $x$ in this case.\n\nThe next step is to solve for $x$ in the second equation $bx - 10 = -2$. Adding 10 to both sides then gives $bx = 8$. Dividing both sides by $b$ then gives us $x = \\frac{8}{b}$. Since we know that $x = -2$ in this case, we can equate the two forms of $x$ in the two equations to get $-2 = \\frac{8}{b}$.\n\nEvaluating this equation,\n\\begin{align}\n&-2 = \\frac{8}{b} \\\\[5pt]\n\\implies &2b = 8 \\\\[5pt]\n\\implies &b = \\boxed{4}.\n\\end{align}\n\nThus, $b$ is equal to 4.",
